    {
      "id": "g6q6ys3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) serves as the central monetary authority responsible for credit control and organizational regulation.",
        "Key monetary policy instruments include the Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF) and Marginal Standing Facility (MSF).",
        "The Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) governs the inflation targeting framework to maintain price stability.",
        "RBI oversees Non-Banking Financial Companies (NBFCs) and regulates digital payment systems in India.",
        "Basel Norms define capital adequacy standards and risk regulation guidelines enforced across banks."
      ],
      "id": "01qaq0x"
    },
