          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bmc0ufx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. LIQUIDITY ADJUSTMENT FACILITY (LAF)"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Monetary Instrument / Concept",
        "Primary Objective"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF)",
          "Manages day-to-day liquidity mismatches through repo and reverse repo transactions."
        ],
        [
          "Marginal Standing Facility (MSF)",
          "Provides penal rate overnight liquidity borrowing window for scheduled commercial banks."
        ],
        [
          "Monetary Policy Committee (MPC)",
          "Determines benchmark policy interest rates to meet explicit inflation targets."
        ],
        [
          "Basel Norms",
          "Establishes international capital adequacy and risk mitigation standards for banks."
        ]
      ],
      "id": "fscwmn3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cw3ek74",
      "content": "LAF was introduced in 2000 to manage short-term liquidity in the banking system."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "93w3jnt",
      "content": "It operates through Repo Rate and Reverse Repo Rate."
    },
    {
      "id": "6f5jq6k",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Instrument</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Impact</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Repo Rate</p>",
            "<p>RBI lends to banks</p>",
            "<p>Controls inflation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Reverse Repo</p>",
            "<p>Banks deposit money with RBI</p>",
            "<p>Absorbs liquidity</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "xq26j1k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. MARGINAL STANDING FACILITY (MSF)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0fqurmk",
      "content": "MSF was introduced in 2011. It allows banks to borrow overnight funds from RBI against government securities beyond SLR limit."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8fxcmcr",
      "content": "MSF rate is usually higher than Repo Rate."
    },
    {
      "id": "rmczhcd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. BASEL NORMS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1mmu3j3",
      "content": "Basel Norms are international banking regulations issued by Basel Committee on Banking Supervision (BCBS)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gem9vc6",
      "content": "Objective: Strengthen bank capital adequacy and risk management."
    },
    {
      "id": "k3y47aj",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Basel Accord</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Focus</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Basel I (1988)</p>",
            "<p>Credit risk</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Basel II</p>",
            "<p>Risk management framework</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Basel III</p>",
            "<p>Stronger capital &amp; liquidity norms</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ae8aynw",
      "content": "India follows Basel III norms."
    },
    {
      "id": "n5gr6d7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. NBFC (NON-BANKING FINANCIAL COMPANY) REGULATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "onbvabf",
      "content": "NBFCs provide banking-like services but do not have full banking license."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "spct1hz",
      "content": "They cannot accept demand deposits like commercial banks."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Understand the key operational differences between Liquidity Adjustment Facility (LAF) and Marginal Standing Facility (MSF).",
        "Memorize the composition and function of the Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) under the Inflation Targeting Framework.",
        "Study RBI's regulatory supervision rules regarding NBFCs, Basel Norms, and digital payment systems."
      ],
      "id": "w0h1khx"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hif04fd",
      "content": "RBI regulates NBFCs under RBI Act, 1934."
    },
